  <heading level="2">Add and Subtract Polynomials</heading>
  <paragraph>We can think of adding and subtracting polynomials as just adding and subtracting a series of monomials. Look for the like terms—those with the same variables and the same exponent. The Commutative Property allows us to rearrange the terms to put like terms together.</paragraph>
  <example number="6.7">
    <problem>
      <paragraph>Find the sum: $$\left( {5y^{2} - 3y + 15} \right) + \left( {3y^{2} - 4y - 11} \right).$$</paragraph>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <cell>Identify like terms.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Rearrange to get the like terms together.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Combine like terms.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </solution>
  </example>
